    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d946">

                <pb facs="0846" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2990.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-01T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1912—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A telegram from consul at Chihuahua via El Paso, dated February 29, states
                    Americans at Velardena, besieged since 23d, had a fight with rebels on 27th,
                    driving them off, but that the need of immediate protection or escort to Torreón
                    is imperative.</p>
                <p>Immediately and most urgently represent to Mexican Government that the needs of
                    Americans at Velardena must be given preference and that an adequate force be
                    sent at once to their relief.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
